  "generated_text": "First, we need to simplify the function \\( f(x) = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} \\).\n\nNotice that:\n\\[\nf(x) = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = \\frac{1 + x}{1 - 3x} = -1\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( f(x) = -1 \\).\n\nTherefore, \\( f_{1993}(3) \\) simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[-1, '-1']",
    "gold_answer": "$f(3) = \\frac{1 + 3}{1 - 3\\cdot 3} = -\\frac{1}{2}$. Then $f_1(3) = f(-\\frac12) = \\frac{1 - \\frac12}{1 + 3\\cdot\\frac12} = \\frac15$, $\\displaystyle f_2(3) = f(\\frac15) = \\frac{1 + \\frac15}{1 - 3\\cdot\\frac15} = 3$ and $f_3(3) = f(3) = \\frac{1 + 3}{1 - 3\\cdot 3} = -\\frac{1}{2}$.\nIt follows immediately that the function cycles and $f_n(3) = -\\frac12$ if $n = 3k$, $f_n(3) = \\frac15$ if $n = 3k + 1$ and $f_n(3) = 3$ if $n = 3k + 2$. Since $1993 = 3\\cdot 664 + 1$, $f_{1993}(3) = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}$.",
    "is_correct": false
  },
